Outcomes, scope, data, and working plan for the upcoming build 

Core message: This code-a-thon is intended to produce functional first prototypes of a patient-education chat experience and perioperative care companions, while also creating initial interfaces for Voice of Customer data, call-transcript data, and our experiment portfolio/results. In parallel, we will establish the evaluation, discovery, and insight practices needed to improve these experiences. The initial prototypes are for controlled clinician/care-team evaluation using live data—not patient-facing deployment. 

1. What We Want to Accomplish 

By the end of the code-a-thon, we should have tangible, testable prototype versions of the three core product outcomes, plus three enabling interfaces for Voice of Customer data, call-transcript data, and experiment data/results. Together, these outputs should give us both working experiences and a stronger foundation for evaluation, discovery, insights, and continued experimentation. 

